<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kawus (son of Kavad I)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 531</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kawus was the eldest son of the Sasanian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kavad-i">Kavad I</a> and ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a> and the Caspian provinces as a sub-king in the early 6th century. When his younger brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-i">Khosrow I</a> was chosen to succeed their father in 531, Kawus claimed the throne and was defeated and executed. Later dynasties of Tabaristan, such as the Bavandids, claimed descent from him.</p></div>
